Subject: [PATCH] Preserve exact ELF shared-library artifacts in Rust linking

Upstream: https://github.com/hermeticbuild/rules_rust/tree/fb6108715c7e1ab6b0c78b37aef2388e5aeb7cc3
Reason: CcInfo can provide versioned, non-lib-prefixed, or same-basename ELF
interface artifacts. Inferring an unversioned -l name loses that identity.
Pass the declared artifact path to the native linker after the Rust archives,
matching C++ linkage and preserving the ELF SONAME. The late position also
keeps --as-needed from dropping DSOs before their Rust references appear.
Runtime search paths use the actual DSO instead of its interface artifact.
This allows ordinary rustc linking with panic=abort and cross-crate full LTO.
Platform-specific Darwin and Windows link arguments stay unchanged.

diff --git a/rust/private/rustc.bzl b/rust/private/rustc.bzl
--- a/rust/private/rustc.bzl
+++ b/rust/private/rustc.bzl
@@ -3110,7 +3110,9 @@
         return depset([])
 
     dylibs = [
-        get_preferred_artifact(lib, use_pic)
+        # Interface libraries are link-time artifacts. The loader needs the
+        # runtime DSO, which can have a different filename and directory.
+        lib.dynamic_library or get_preferred_artifact(lib, use_pic)
         for linker_input in dep_info.transitive_noncrates.to_list()
         for lib in linker_input.libraries
         if _is_dylib(lib)
@@ -3448,6 +3450,13 @@
                 ("-Clink-arg=%s" % get_preferred_artifact(lib, use_pic).path),
                 ("-Clink-arg=%s--no-whole-archive" % prefix),
             ])
+        elif include_link_flags and _is_dylib(lib):
+            # Preserve the exact ELF artifact (including interface libraries).
+            # Inferring -l names loses versions and cannot distinguish equal
+            # basenames in separate directories. Pass it after Rust archives,
+            # so --as-needed sees their references before considering the DSO.
+            artifact = get_preferred_artifact(lib, use_pic)
+            ret.append("-Clink-arg=%s" % artifact.path)
         elif include_link_flags:
             ret.extend(portable_link_flags(lib, use_pic, ambiguous_libs, get_lib_name_default))
     _add_user_link_flags(ret, linker_input)
